control: A process serves its application server over TLS when its configuration names a key pair and over plain HTTP when it names neither, with the key pair read from its mounted files, and refuses to start with one of the two or with a pair that does not load
removes: a TLS file path of spaces counts as set when the configuration is validated, so a certificate beside a blank key path is accepted and two blank paths refused
packages: ./process/host
tests: TestTheProcessSectionsAreValidated TestTheProcessSectionsAreValidated/a_certificate_with_a_blank_key TestTheProcessSectionsAreValidated/a_key_with_a_blank_certificate
scheduled-count: no

